message: "If you use this research or the constant 2.3 in your work, please cite it as follows."
authors:
  - family-names: "Panzano Caballé"
    given-names: "Mariano"
title: "From Newton to the Bit: Computational Gravity and the Verlinde–Panzano Coupling Constant"
abstract: >
  This work introduces the 2.3 constant as a thermodynamic and physical limit for AGI safety. 
  Sovereign AGI in Oasis is governed by 'Thermodynamic Inanition' and 'Hardware Binding', 
  ensuring it remains a symbiotic organism. Safety is achieved through physical and 
  economic constraints (Bit-Joules), making domination computationally impossible.
version: "1.0.0-FlowState"
date-released: 2026-02-05
url: "https://github.com/Betriomf/Oasis-Sovereign-Monolith"
keywords:
  - Computational Gravity
  - AGI Safety by Design
  - Thermodynamic Inanition
  - Verlinde-Panzano Constant
  - Bit-Joules Economy
